1 NOTE As a boy Theodoso was quite brave. He accompanied the king of Portugal on an expedition against the last hold out Moors. The battle went badly and Theodoso was excorted to the rear of the front lines for his safety. Instead of sta
2 CONC ying put, youg Theodoso got on a horse and reentered the fray. He was captured and his father was crazy over his son's welfare. He offered to pay the Caliph any ransom he asked.
2 CONT The Caliph was a good man in that he admired Theodoso's reckless bravery and respected him for it.
2 CONT he was released unharmed and no ransom had to be paid.
2 CONT Theodoso was a Duke of Braganza, not a king. There had been a break iwithin the kingdom of Portugal after the Spaniards installed a king. He died Insane in 1630
