1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Juan Manuel Pérez de Guzmán y Silva (1579-1636), VIII duque de Medina Sidonia, XI Conde de Niebla y XIII Señor de Sanlúcar. Noble español perteneciente a la Casa de Medina-Sidonia, hijo de Alonso Pérez de Guzmán el
2 CONC  Bueno y Zúñiga, VIII Duque de Medina-Sidonia y Ana de Silva y Mendoza, hija de la Princesa de Éboli. Casó en 1598, con Juana de Sandoval, hija del Duque de Lerma, valido de Felipe III, matrimonio del que nacieron, entre otros, Lu
2 CONC isa de Guzmán, futura reina consorte y regente de Portugal, Alonso Pérez de Guzmán XII Conde de Niebla y Gaspar Pérez de Guzmán y Sandoval, IX Duque de Medina-Sidonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Manuel Domingo Francifco de Paula Perez de Guzman, es llamado de otros Don Manuel Alonfo, Don Juan Manuel y Don Manuel Francifco, octavo Duque de Medina-Sydonia, fexto Conde de Niebla, Marques de Cazaza, cafó con Doña Juana de
2 CONC  Sandoval, hija mayor de Don Francifco de Sandoval y Roxas, primer Duque, y quinto Conde de Lerma, quinto Marques de Denia, y defpues Cardenal. Historia de la Muy Ilustre Casa de Sousa España, 1770. Casa de los Duques de Medina-Sy
2 CONC donia. Pág. 382
2 CONT
2 CONT == Links ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books/about/%C3%81rboles_de_Costados_de_Gran_Parte_de_La.html?id=7Nv3ygAACAAJ Árboles de Costados de Gran Parte de Las Primeras Casas de Estos Reynos: Cuyos Dueños Vivian en El Año De 1683]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Manuel_P%C3%A9rez_de_Guzm%C3%A1n,_8th_Duke_of_Medina_Sidonia
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Manuel Pérez de Guzmán y Silva (7 January 1579 – 1636), was a Spanish noble and 8th Duke of Medina Sidonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Alonso Pérez de Guzmán, 7th Duke of Medina Sidonia, commander-in-chief of the Spanish Armada and Ana de Silva y Mendoza, daughter of Ana de Mendoza, Princess of Éboli.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He married in 1598, aged 19, Juana de Sandoval, daughter of the Duke of Lerma, a favourite of Philip III of Spain. He was promoted to Knight of the Order of the Golden Fleece in 1615, aged 36 and 34 years after his father. In the
2 CONC  same year he became 8th Duke of Medina Sidonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1625 he commanded, from Jerez de la Frontera, the military operations neutralizing the attack on Cadiz by a Dutch-English Fleet, commanded by Sir Edward Cecil.
2 CONT
2 CONT His eldest daughter Luisa de Guzman (1613–1666), became queen-consort of Portugal when her husband John II, 8th Duke of Braganza became John IV, the first King of Portugal of the House of Braganza in 1640. In order to encourage he
2 CONC r husband when the Portuguese nobility offered him the crown of Portugal, Luisa is known for her phrase: "better Queen for one day, than Duchess all my life".
2 CONT
2 CONT His granddaughter Catherine of Braganza, married King Charles II of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
