2 CONT ===Dukes of Escalona===
2 CONT * Duke of Escalona is a Spanish noble title given by '''Henry IV of Castile''' in 1472 to Juan Pacheco, first Marquis of Villena. The name Escalona refers to the village Escalona del Alberche, in the Province of Toledo. The Dukes 
2 CONC of Escalona remained an important family throughout the Spanish history. Charles III of Spain made Juan Pacheco, 11th Duke-consort of Escalona a Grandee of Spain first class in 1750. The Dukes of Escalona had many other titles, in
2 CONC cluding : Marquis of Villena, Count of Xiquena, Count of San Esteban de Gormaz, Count of Castañeda, etc.. Don Juan Pacheco, 1st Duke of Escalona (1419–1474) Don Diego Lopez de Pacheco, 2nd Duke of Escalona (1456-1529) Don Diego Ló
2 CONC pez Pacheco, 3rd Duke of Escalona (1506-1556) Don Francisco Pacheco, 4th Duke of Escalona (1532-1574) Don Juan Fernandez Pacheco, 5th Duke of Escalona (1563-1615) Don Felipe Fernández Pacheco, 6th Duke of Escalona (1596-1633) Don 
2 CONC Diego López Pacheco, 7th Duke of Escalona (1599-1653) Don Juan Manuel López de Pacheco, 8th Duke of Escalona (1650-1725) Don Mercurio López Pacheco, 9th Duke of Escalona (1679-1738) Don Andrés Fernández Pacheco, 10th Duke of Escal
2 CONC ona (1710-1746) Doña María Ana López Pacheco Toledo y Portugal, 11th Duchess of Escalona (1729-1768) '''Don Felipe Lopez-Pacheco de La Cueva, 12th Duke of Escalona (1727-1798)''' Don Diego López Pacheco Téllez-Girón Gómez de Sando
2 CONC val, 13th Duke of Escalona (1754-1811) Don Bernardino Fernández de Velasco, 14th Duke of Escalona (1783-1851)
