1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Antonio Spinola Ponce de León y Spínola de la Cerda, 
2 CONT 11th Duke of Arcos, 1st Duke of Baños, VIII [Portuguese] Duke of Aveiro.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT After serving as a military officer in Italy, in 1752 he returned to Spain and was appointed supernumerary captain of the Spanish Company of Royal Guards of Corps. In December 1763 he succeeded his brother Francis in the Duchy of 
2 CONC Arcos, and the following year he was awarded the Golden Fleece. In 1772 he was appointed by Charles III Captain General of the Royal Armies, although he remained in command of the Corps Guards.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married on 1 January 1778 to Mariana de Silva-Bazán and Sarmiento, mother of the celebrated Duchess of Alba, with whom she had no offspring.
2 CONT
2 CONT With his death, in 1780, he finished the firstborn male line of the Ponce de León, and the house of Arcos was incorporated into the house of Benavente, and later to the house of Osuna until 2016 that regains its independence. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonio_Ponce_de_Le%C3%B3n '''es.wikipedia''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Antonio Ponce de León, XI Duque de Arcos (1726 – 13 de diciembre de 1780), noble y militar español, I duque de Baños y VIII duque de Aveiro, en Portugal.  Tras servir como militar en Italia, en 1752 regresó a España y fue nombrado
2 CONC  capitán supernum
2 CONT
2 CONT Update Dec 2021 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Casó el 1 de enero de 1778 con Mariana de Silva-Bazán y Sarmiento, madre de la célebre duquesa de Alba, con la que no tuvo descendencia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Con su muerte, en 1780, acabó la línea masculina primogénita de los Ponce de León, y la Casa de Arcos quedó incorporada a la Casa de Benavente, y posteriormente a la Casa de Osuna hasta 2016 que recupera su independencia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====English translation====
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Antonio Ponce de Leon, Duke of Arcos XI (1726 - December 13, 1780), Spanish nobleman and military, Duke of Baths I and VIII Duke of Aveiro, Portugal.
2 CONT * After serving as a soldier in Italy, in 1752 returned to Spain and was named captain of the Spanish Company supernumerary of Royal Guards Corps. In December 1763 he succeeded his brother Francis in the duchy of Arcos, and the fo
2 CONC llowing year,  he was awarded '''the Golden Fleece''' in 1772 by Charles III was appointed Captain General of the Royal Army, but continued in command of the Guards Corps .
2 CONT * With his death, in 1780, finished the eldest male line of the Ponce de Leon, and Casa de Arcos was incoporada to the House of Osuna. Was the 11th Duke of Arcos  
2 CONT * 1st  wife was Maria Luisa who was daughter of King Philip V [NO]
2 CONT * 2nd wife was the Duchess of Huescar 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Update Dec 2021
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 January 1778, he married Mariana de Silva-Bazán y Sarmiento, mother of the famous María Cayetana de Silva, 13th Duchess of Alba, with whom he had no descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT With his death on 13 December 1780, the first-born male line of the House of Ponce de León became extinct, and the House of Arcos was incorporated into the House of Benavente, and later to the House of Osuna.
2 CONT
2 CONT ><><><><><<><<><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>  
2 CONT
2 CONT Duque de Arcos, Nágera, Maqueda, y Baños, Marqués de Zahara, y Elche, Conde de Baylén, de Casares, Treviño, y Valencia de D. Juan, Grande de España de primera Clase, Adelantado mayor del Reyno de Granada, Capitan General de los Re
2 CONC ales Exércitos, Gentil-Hombre de Cámara con Exercicio, Capitan de la Compañía Española de Reales Guardias de Corps, Caballero del Toysón, Gran Cruz de la Real Distinguida Orden Española de Carlos III y Comendador de Calzadilla en 
2 CONC la de Santiago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duque de Baños, y Aveyro, Gentil Hombre de Camara de S.M. con exercicio, Cavallero del orden de Santiago, Comendador de Calzadilla, Mariscal de Campo, y Edecan del Serenisimo Señor Infante D. Felipe, en cuyo servicio ha proseguido
2 CONC  desempeñando sus obligaciones despues de la meurte de sus dos hermanos. Casa de Cabrera en Córdoba, P. Francisco Ruano Libro I, Capítulo XIII, De Don Rodrigo Ponce de Leon, I Duque de Arcos, II Marqués de Zahara, Conde de Casares
2 CONC , VI Señor de Villa Garcia, VIII del estado de Marchena, progenitor de la linea de los Excmos. Duques de ARcos, que se continúa en este Capitulo.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Antonio Ponce de Leon, undecimo Duque de Arcos, decimotercio Marques de Zara y de Maqueda, Teniente General de los Reales Exercitos de fu Mageftad Don Carlos III y Capitan de fus Reales Guardias de Corps de la Compañia Efpañol
2 CONC a. Historia de la Muy Ilustre Casa de Sousa Capitulo XII. Descendencia de Don Garcia Mendez de Sousa en diverfas Cafas por fu hijo Don Juan Garcia de Soufa y fu nieta Doña Elvira. Duques de Arcos.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Antonio Ponce de Leon, hijo de Don Joachin Ponce de Leon y de Doña Ana de Spinola y la Cerda, Duque de Arcos, en quien fe fuprimió dicho Ducado de Aveyro, quedando reunido en la Corona de Portugal. Historia de la Muy Ilustre C
2 CONC asa de Sousa Capitulo XVI. Duques de Aveyro.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Family
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Mar%C3%ADa-Luisa-de-Bourbon-Fictional/6000000001159734669 Was not the daughter  of https://www.geni.com/people/Felipe-V-de-Espa%C3%B1a/5318340685370041549?through=6000000001159734669 & not the wife of h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/people/Antonio-Ponce-de-Le%C3%B3n-XI-duque-de-Arcos/6000000001159848184?through=6000000001159734669.  Not the mother of https://www.geni.com/people/Rodrigo-Ponce-de-Leon/6000000001159913137?through=600000000115
2 CONC 9690685 & https://www.geni.com/people/Pablo-Ponce-de-Leon/6000000001159690685?through=6000000001159913137
2 CONT ----
