1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Condado_de_Villanueva_de_las_Achas '''es.wikipedia.org....'''], [http://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlos_Guti%C3%A9rrez_de_los_R%C3%ADos '''es.wikipedia.org....'''], 
2 CONT * Carlos José Francisco de Paula Gutierrez de los Rios and Sarmiento Rohan, I Duke of Fernan Nunez. * Son of Carlos Jose Gutierrez de los Rios, VI Count of Fernan Nunez, and Mary of Slavery Sarmiento de Sotomayor and Caceres. Born
2 CONC  in Lisbon, where his father was ambassador, in 1779. Very young married Maria Vicenta Solis Vignancourt Lasso de la Vega, VI Duchess de Montellano
2 CONT * Comes to occupy the post of ambassador to London and Paris.
2 CONT * He held important diplomatic posts in the Congress of Vienna. His great diplomatic skills earned him the sympathy and favor of Ferdinand VII, who became Duke, the last count and the first Duke of Fernan Nunez.
2 CONT * He died in 1822 in Paris after falling from a horse, the last owner who exercises jurisdiction over the village manor of Fernan Nunez.
2 CONT * In Madrid's Retiro Gardens is the Paseo del Duque de Fernan Nunez, known as Paseo de Coches.
2 CONT * <><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><
2 CONT * [http://pt.encydia.com/es/Carlos_Guti%C3%A9rrez_dos_Rios '''pt.encydia.com... '''], 
2 CONT * English translation: 
2 CONT * Francisco de Paula Gutierrez Carlos Gutierrez and Sarmiento Rohan Rivers, I Duke of Fernan Nunez. 
2 CONT * Son of Carlos José Gutiérrez Rivers, VI Count of Fernan Nunez, and Maria Sarmiento de Sotomayor of Slavery and Caceres. Born in Lisbon, where his father was ambassador in 1779. 
2 CONT * While very young he married '''María Vicenta Solis Vignancourt Lasso de la Vega''', VI Duchess de Montellano
2 CONT * Enough to occupy the post of ambassador in London and Paris.
2 CONT * Played important diplomatic posts in the Congress of Vienna. His great diplomatic skill gained him the sympathy and favor of Ferdinand VII, who granted him the titles of Duke, the last Earl and first Duke of Fernan Nunez.
2 CONT * He died in 1822 in the French capital after falling from a horse, the latter Holder that exercises jurisdiction over the satately Villa de Fernan Nunez.
2 CONT * Carlos José Francisco de Paula Gutierrez de los Rios and Sarmiento Rohan, I Duke of Fernan Nunez. Son of Carlos Jose Gutierrez de los Rios, VI Count of Fernan Nunez, and Mary of Slavery Sarmiento de Sotomayor and Caceres. Born i
2 CONC n Lisbon, where his father was ambassador, in 1779. Very young married Maria Vicenta Solis Vignancourt Lasso de la Vega, VI Duchess de Montellano
2 CONT =====Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch=====
