1 NOTE 13th Duchess of Alba
2 CONT Died of Fever.
2 CONT Patroness of the painter, Goya. Maria del Pilar Teresa Cayetana de Silva de Toledo was also a humanitarian who was very active in helping the poor. She was ahead of her time because she was a very liberated woman. It is said that 
2 CONC she and Goya were romantically involved. From the clues that are within his paintings of her I think he was madly in love with her. I really can't say if she returned the emotion.
2 CONT In the paintings that I have chosen to set up here Maria points downwards to Goya's name inscribed in the sand. In the painting that she is wearing a beautiful black dress she wears a gold ring that has been inscribed with Goya's 
2 CONC name, "Solo Goya." In my painting of her, The duchess of Alba and Mona Lisa Revisited in the New Millenium I have her standing with her back to the viewer. She points to my name inscribed on the blue wall, "Solo Ayes." Both his wo
2 CONC rks and mine are works ahead of their time.
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT GF Cokayne with Vicary Gibbs H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, Editors, The Complete Peereage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Bitain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant
2 CONC , New Edit:, 13 Volumes in 14 (1910-1959) Reprint in 6 Volumes, Glaucester UK. Alan Sutton Publishing 2000 Volume II page 165 The Complete Peerage.
