0 @N6000000002322303620@ NOTE Maria attempted to correct the harshness dealt by her father's minister. She
1 CONT freed political prisoners, abandoned some of his enterprises and developed
1 CONT small industries in Portugal and new crops in Brazil. Later, the deaths of
1 CONT Peter, son Joseph, and news of the French Revolution so affected her that she
1 CONT suffered mental collapse in January 1792. Son John became regent for her in
1 CONT 1799. Maria proved incapable of resuming her duties when Napoleon's armies
1 CONT invaded Portugal in November 1807, when the royal family escaped to Brazil.
